 ## Subtopics
 
+### [Transparent Voxel Rendering with Refraction](8631-transparent-voxel-rendering-with-refraction.md)
+Extends sparse voxel grid traversal by accumulating color and opacity for transparent voxels while applying Snell's law at material boundaries. It distinguishes itself from opaque traversal by continuing the ray after interaction and from non-refractive transparency by modifying the ray vector. Choose it when rendering semi-transparent refractive media (e.g., glass, water) within a hierarchical voxel structure.
+
 ## Operating characteristics
 **Time and Memory Complexity**
-*   **Time**: The refraction calculation itself is $O(1)$ per voxel entry. However, if TIR is not handled, it can lead to infinite loops, effectively $O(\infty)$ [S1, unofficial]. With the fallback, it remains $O(1)$ but may cause the ray to re-traverse previously visited voxels if the fallback direction is suboptimal, potentially increasing traversal time [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory**: No additional memory is required beyond the ray state variables [S1, unofficial].
